'''''Daniatrogon''''' is an [[extinct]] genus of [[trogon]] bird known from the early [[Eocene]] ([[Ypresian]] age) of Denmark. The genus contains a [[monotypic taxon|single species]], '''''Daniatrogon kochi''''', known from a well-preserved, nearly complete skeleton. The highly elongated [[hallux]] of ''Daniatrogon'' suggests that it and other [[stem group]] trogoniforms were much more mobile whilst they were foraging, contrasting with the sedentary foraging habits of extant trogonids.<ref name="Daniatrogon" />

